## Defining a Type Invariant

```xiom
pub type PositiveInt = Int
  invariant: this > 0;
```

Every PositiveInt must be > 0. The invariant is checked when a value is created or mutated.

### Struct Invariants
```xiom
pub type Rectangle = {
  width: Float64;
  height: Float64;
} invariant: this.width > 0.0 && this.height > 0.0;
```

### Complex Multi-Field Invariants
```xiom
pub type Date = {
  year: Int;
  month: Int;
  day: Int;
} invariant: this.year >= 1;
  invariant: this.month >= 1 && this.month <= 12;
  invariant: this.day >= 1 && this.day <= 31;
  invariant: this.valid_date();
```

### Invariant for Domain Types
```xiom
pub type Email = Str
  invariant: this.contains("@");

pub type PhoneNumber = Str
  invariant: this.len() >= 10;
```

### The Guarantee
```xiom
fn send_email(to: &Email, body: Str) {
  // NO need to check if to contains "@" — the invariant guarantees it!
  io.println("Sending to: " + to);
}
```

Every function receiving an Email knows it's valid — no defensive checks needed.

